subproblem.statement:
Let q, q0 be linear isometries of R^{n+l} and T0 := rotatedPlane q0. Let v : R^n -> R^l, y in R^{n+l}, c in R^n and d in R^l with y = q0(graphPoint c d). Let r > 0, 0 <= eps <= 1/24 and 0 <= vartheta <= 1/12. Assume:
- v is C^1 on the closed ball B_r(0) and v(0) = 0;
- the operator norm of fderivWithin v B_r(0) x is <= eps for every x in B_r(0);
- infDist(q(graphPoint x 0), T0) <= vartheta |x| for every x in R^n.
Then there is f : R^n -> R^l such that:
(a) f is C^1 on the open ball B°_{r/2}(c), and |fderiv f w| <= 1/7 there;
(b) for every w in the closed ball B_{r/2}(c) there is x in B_r(0) with y + q(graphPoint x (v x)) = q0(graphPoint w (f w)) and |graphPoint x (v x)| <= r;
(c) if x is in B_r(0), w is in B_{r/2}(c), b is in R^l, and y + q(graphPoint x (v x)) = q0(graphPoint w b), then b = f(w).
